{"id":"mahabharata-5-089","work":"mahabharata","part":5,"partName":"उद्योगपर्व","partNameEn":"Udyoga Parva","unit":89,"title":"एकोननवतितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 89 · Krishna refuses Duryodhana's food","summary":{"en":"Krishna goes to Duryodhana's palace, but declines his invitation to dine, saying envoys eat only when their mission succeeds, and that one eats another's food only out of love or need, neither of which applies. He returns to Vidura's house and eats there with his companions.","kn":"ಶ್ರೀಕೃಷ್ಣನು ದುರ್ಯೋಧನನ ಅರಮನೆಗೆ ಹೋಗುತ್ತಾನೆ, ಆದರೆ ದೂತರು ಕಾರ್ಯಸಿದ್ಧಿಯಾದಾಗ ಮಾತ್ರ ಊಟ ಮಾಡುತ್ತಾರೆ, ಪ್ರೀತಿಯಿಂದ ಅಥವಾ ಆಪತ್ತಿನಿಂದ ಮಾತ್ರ ಪರರ ಅನ್ನ ಉಣ್ಣಬೇಕು, ಇಲ್ಲಿ ಎರಡೂ ಇಲ್ಲ ಎಂದು ಭೋಜನದ ಆಹ್ವಾನ ನಿರಾಕರಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ. ವಿದುರನ ಮನೆಗೆ ಮರಳಿ ಸಂಗಡಿಗರೊಂದಿಗೆ ಅಲ್ಲಿ ಊಟ ಮಾಡುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"श्रीकृष्ण दुर्योधन के महल जाते हैं, पर भोजन का निमन्त्रण अस्वीकार करते हुए कहते हैं कि दूत कार्य सफल होने पर ही भोजन करते हैं, और दूसरे का अन्न प्रेम से या विपत्ति में ही खाया जाता है, और यहाँ दोनों नहीं हैं। वे विदुर के घर लौटकर साथियों के साथ वहीं भोजन करते हैं।","te":"శ్రీకృష్ణుడు దుర్యోధనుని భవనానికి వెళ్తాడు, కానీ దూతలు కార్యసిద్ధి అయినప్పుడే భోజనం చేస్తారని, ప్రేమతో లేదా ఆపదలో మాత్రమే ఇతరుల అన్నం తినాలని, ఇక్కడ రెండూ లేవని భోజన ఆహ్వానాన్ని నిరాకరిస్తాడు. విదురుని ఇంటికి తిరిగివచ్చి సహచరులతో అక్కడ భోజనం చేస్తాడు.","ta":"ஸ்ரீகிருஷ்ணர் துரியோதனனின் அரண்மனைக்குச் செல்கிறார், ஆனால் தூதர்கள் பணி நிறைவேறியபோதே உண்பார்கள், அன்பினாலோ ஆபத்திலோ மட்டுமே பிறர் உணவை உண்ண வேண்டும், இங்கு இரண்டும் இல்லை என்று உணவு அழைப்பை மறுக்கிறார். விதுரரின் இல்லம் திரும்பித் தோழர்களுடன் அங்கு உணவருந்துகிறார்.","ml":"ദുര്യോധനന്റെ കൊട്ടാരത്തിൽ ചെന്ന കൃഷ്ണൻ അവന്റെ ഭക്ഷണക്ഷണം നിരസിക്കുന്നു; ദൂതന്മാർ തങ്ങളുടെ ദൗത്യം വിജയിക്കുമ്പോൾ മാത്രമേ ഭക്ഷിക്കൂ എന്ന് അദ്ദേഹം പറയുന്നു. സ്നേഹംകൊണ്ടോ ആവശ്യംകൊണ്ടോ മാത്രമേ മറ്റൊരാളുടെ ഭക്ഷണം കഴിക്കാവൂ, ഇവയിലൊന്നും ഇവിടെ ബാധകമല്ല. അദ്ദേഹം വിദുരരുടെ വീട്ടിൽ മടങ്ങിയെത്തി, കൂട്ടാളികളോടൊപ്പം അവിടെ ഭക്ഷണം കഴിക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 5.89; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Jan 23 2024","sections":[{"title":"भगवद्यानपर्व","titleEn":"Bhagavadyana Parva (Krishna's embassy)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"पृथामामन्त्र्य गोविन्दः कृत्वा चापि प्रदक्षिणम् ।\nदुर्योधनगृहं शौरिरभ्यगच्छदरिंदमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having taken leave of Pritha and circled her, Govinda, Shauri, subduer of foes, went to Duryodhana's house."}},{"n":2,"text":"लक्ष्म्या परमया युक्तं पुरंदरगृहोपमम् ।\nतस्य कक्ष्या व्यतिक्रम्य तिस्रो द्वाःस्थैरवारितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"It was full of supreme splendor, like the house of Indra; unstopped by doorkeepers, he passed through its three courtyards."}},{"n":3,"text":"ततोऽभ्रघनसंकाशं गिरिकूटमिवोच्छ्रितम् ।\nश्रिया ज्वलन्तं प्रासादमारुरोह महायशाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the very renowned one climbed to the palace, tall as a mountain peak, dense as a cloud and blazing with splendor."}},{"n":4,"text":"तत्र राजसहस्रैश्च कुरुभिश्चाभिसंवृतम् ।\nधार्तराष्ट्रं महाबाहुं ददर्शासीनमासने ॥","meaning":{"en":"There he saw the mighty-armed Dhartarashtra seated on a throne, surrounded by thousands of kings and the Kurus."}},{"n":5,"text":"दुःशासनं च कर्णं च शकुनिं चापि सौबलम् ।\nदुर्योधनसमीपे तानासनस्थान्ददर्श सः ॥","meaning":{"en":"He saw Duhshasana, Karna and Shakuni, son of Subala, seated near Duryodhana."}},{"n":6,"text":"अभ्यागच्छति दाशार्हे धार्तराष्ट्रो महायशाः ।\nउदतिष्ठत्सहामात्यः पूजयन्मधुसूदनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As Dasharha approached, the renowned Dhartarashtra rose with his ministers, honoring Madhusudana."}},{"n":7,"text":"समेत्य धार्तराष्ट्रेण सहामात्येन केशवः ।\nराजभिस्तत्र वार्ष्णेयः समागच्छद्यथावयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Meeting Dhartarashtra and his ministers, Keshava met the kings there in order of age."}},{"n":8,"text":"तत्र जाम्बूनदमयं पर्यङ्कं सुपरिष्कृतम् ।\nविविधास्तरणास्तीर्णमभ्युपाविशदच्युतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There Achyuta sat on a golden couch, well furnished and spread with various coverings."}},{"n":9,"text":"तस्मिन्गां मधुपर्कं च उपहृत्य जनार्दने ।\nनिवेदयामास तदा गृहान्राज्यं च कौरवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"After offering Janardana a cow and a honey-offering, the Kaurava then presented his houses and kingdom."}},{"n":10,"text":"तत्र गोविन्दमासीनं प्रसन्नादित्यवर्चसम् ।\nउपासां चक्रिरे सर्वे कुरवो राजभिः सह ॥","meaning":{"en":"As Govinda sat there, bright as the clear sun, all the Kurus and kings waited upon him."}},{"n":11,"text":"ततो दुर्योधनो राजा वार्ष्णेयं जयतां वरम् ।\nन्यमन्त्रयद्भोजनेन नाभ्यनन्दच्च केशवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then King Duryodhana invited Varshneya, best of victors, to a meal, but Keshava did not accept."}},{"n":12,"text":"ततो दुर्योधनः कृष्णमब्रवीद्राजसंसदि ।\nमृदुपूर्वं शठोदर्कं कर्णमाभाष्य कौरवः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then in the royal assembly Duryodhana, the Kaurava, spoke to Krishna, first gently and with a crafty end, having turned to Karna."}},{"n":13,"text":"कस्मादन्नानि पानानि वासांसि शयनानि च ।\nत्वदर्थमुपनीतानि नाग्रहीस्त्वं जनार्दन ॥","meaning":{"en":"Janardana, why did you not accept the foods, drinks, garments and beds brought for you?"}},{"n":14,"text":"उभयोश्चाददः साह्यमुभयोश्च हिते रतः ।\nसंबन्धी दयितश्चासि धृतराष्ट्रस्य माधव ॥","meaning":{"en":"You help both sides and delight in the good of both; you are a kinsman and dear to Dhritarashtra, Madhava."}},{"n":15,"text":"त्वं हि गोविन्द धर्मार्थौ वेत्थ तत्त्वेन सर्वशः ।\nतत्र कारणमिच्छामि श्रोतुं चक्रगदाधर ॥","meaning":{"en":"Govinda, you know dharma and profit in truth and in all things; I wish to hear the reason, bearer of discus and mace."}},{"n":16,"text":"स एवमुक्तो गोविन्दः प्रत्युवाच महामनाः ।\nओघमेघस्वनः काले प्रगृह्य विपुलं भुजम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus addressed, great-minded Govinda replied, raising his large arm, his voice like a flood-laden cloud."}},{"n":17,"text":"अनम्बूकृतमग्रस्तमनिरस्तमसंकुलम् ।\nराजीवनेत्रो राजानं हेतुमद्वाक्यमुत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The lotus-eyed one spoke to the king these excellent words, reasoned, not muffled, not swallowed, not disconnected, not confused."}},{"n":18,"text":"कृतार्था भुञ्जते दूताः पूजां गृह्णन्ति चैव हि ।\nकृतार्थं मां सहामात्यस्त्वमर्चिष्यसि भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Messengers eat and accept honor only when their errand is done; when my purpose is done, you may honor me with your ministers, Bharata."}},{"n":19,"text":"एवमुक्तः प्रत्युवाच धार्तराष्ट्रो जनार्दनम् ।\nन युक्तं भवतास्मासु प्रतिपत्तुमसांप्रतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus addressed, Dhartarashtra replied to Janardana: It is not right for you to treat us so inappropriately."}},{"n":20,"text":"कृतार्थं चाकृतार्थं च त्वां वयं मधुसूदन ।\nयतामहे पूजयितुं गोविन्द न च शक्नुमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whether your errand is done or not, Madhusudana, we try to honor you, Govinda, but we do not succeed."}},{"n":21,"text":"न च तत्कारणं विद्मो यस्मिन्नो मधुसूदन ।\nपूजां कृतां प्रीयमाणैर्नामंस्थाः पुरुषोत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"We do not know the reason, Madhusudana, why you, best of men, did not accept the honor offered by us with affection."}},{"n":22,"text":"वैरं नो नास्ति भवता गोविन्द न च विग्रहः ।\nस भवान्प्रसमीक्ष्यैतन्नेदृशं वक्तुमर्हति ॥","meaning":{"en":"We have no enmity with you, Govinda, nor any quarrel; considering this, you should not speak like this."}},{"n":23,"text":"एवमुक्तः प्रत्युवाच धार्तराष्ट्रं जनार्दनः ।\nअभिवीक्ष्य सहामात्यं दाशार्हः प्रहसन्निव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus addressed, Janardana, Dasharha, looked at Dhartarashtra with his ministers and spoke, seeming to smile."}},{"n":24,"text":"नाहं कामान्न संरम्भान्न द्वेषान्नार्थकारणात् ।\nन हेतुवादाल्लोभाद्वा धर्मं जह्यां कथंचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"I would never abandon dharma for desire, anger, hatred, gain, argument or greed."}},{"n":25,"text":"संप्रीतिभोज्यान्यन्नानि आपद्भोज्यानि वा पुनः ।\nन च संप्रीयसे राजन्न चाप्यापद्गता वयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Food is to be eaten when given in affection, or when one is in distress; you are not pleased with us, king, and we are not in distress."}},{"n":26,"text":"अकस्माद्द्विषसे राजञ्जन्मप्रभृति पाण्डवान् ।\nप्रियानुवर्तिनो भ्रातॄन्सर्वैः समुदितान्गुणैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, you have hated the Pandavas without cause since your birth, brothers who are loyal and endowed with every virtue."}},{"n":27,"text":"अकस्माच्चैव पार्थानां द्वेषणं नोपपद्यते ।\nधर्मे स्थिताः पाण्डवेयाः कस्तान्किं वक्तुमर्हति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hatred of the Parthas without cause is unreasonable; the Pandavas are established in dharma; who can say anything against them?"}},{"n":28,"text":"यस्तान्द्वेष्टि स मां द्वेष्टि यस्ताननु स मामनु ।\nऐकात्म्यं मां गतं विद्धि पाण्डवैर्धर्मचारिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Whoever hates them hates me; whoever follows them follows me; know that I am one with the Pandavas, who practice dharma."}},{"n":29,"text":"कामक्रोधानुवर्ती हि यो मोहाद्विरुरुत्सते ।\nगुणवन्तं च यो द्वेष्टि तमाहुः पुरुषाधमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who is led by desire and anger, who through delusion seeks to fight, and who hates the virtuous, is called the lowest of men."}},{"n":30,"text":"यः कल्याणगुणाञ्ज्ञातीन्मोहाल्लोभाद्दिदृक्षते ।\nसोऽजितात्माजितक्रोधो न चिरं तिष्ठति श्रियम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"One who out of delusion and greed wishes to see his virtuous relatives harmed, being unsubdued and angry, does not keep prosperity long."}},{"n":31,"text":"अथ यो गुणसंपन्नान्हृदयस्याप्रियानपि ।\nप्रियेण कुरुते वश्यांश्चिरं यशसि तिष्ठति ॥","meaning":{"en":"But one who makes even virtuous people unpleasant to his heart his own by kindness stays long in fame."}},{"n":32,"text":"सर्वमेतदभोक्तव्यमन्नं दुष्टाभिसंहितम् ।\nक्षत्तुरेकस्य भोक्तव्यमिति मे धीयते मतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"All this food, prepared with bad intent, is not to be eaten; my mind holds that only Kshattri's food is to be eaten."}},{"n":33,"text":"एवमुक्त्वा महाबाहुर्दुर्योधनममर्षणम् ।\nनिश्चक्राम ततः शुभ्राद्धार्तराष्ट्रनिवेशनात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said this to the intolerant Duryodhana, the mighty-armed one left that bright house of the Dhartarashtra."}},{"n":34,"text":"निर्याय च महाबाहुर्वासुदेवो महामनाः ।\nनिवेशाय ययौ वेश्म विदुरस्य महात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Leaving, the mighty-armed, great-minded Vasudeva went to stay at the house of great-souled Vidura."}},{"n":35,"text":"तमभ्यगच्छद्द्रोणश्च कृपो भीष्मोऽथ बाह्लिकः ।\nकुरवश्च महाबाहुं विदुरस्य गृहे स्थितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Drona, Kripa, Bhishma and Bahlika, and the Kurus came to the mighty-armed one as he stayed in Vidura's house."}},{"n":36,"text":"तेऽभिगम्याब्रुवंस्तत्र कुरवो मधुसूदनम् ।\nनिवेदयामो वार्ष्णेय सरत्नांस्ते गृहान्वयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Kurus approached Madhusudana and said: Varshneya, we offer you our houses, filled with jewels."}},{"n":37,"text":"तानुवाच महातेजाः कौरवान्मधुसूदनः ।\nसर्वे भवन्तो गच्छन्तु सर्वा मेऽपचितिः कृता ॥","meaning":{"en":"Madhusudana of great splendor said to those Kauravas: All of you may go; all honor has been done to me."}},{"n":38,"text":"यातेषु कुरुषु क्षत्ता दाशार्हमपराजितम् ।\nअभ्यर्चयामास तदा सर्वकामैः प्रयत्नवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the Kurus had gone, Kshattri diligently honored the unconquered Dasharha with every desirable thing."}},{"n":39,"text":"ततः क्षत्तान्नपानानि शुचीनि गुणवन्ति च ।\nउपाहरदनेकानि केशवाय महात्मने ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Kshattri brought many pure and excellent foods and drinks to great-souled Keshava."}},{"n":40,"text":"तैर्तर्पयित्वा प्रथमं ब्राह्मणान्मधुसूदनः ।\nवेदविद्भ्यो ददौ कृष्णः परमद्रविणान्यपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"With them Madhusudana first satisfied the brahmanas, and Krishna gave great wealth to the Veda-knowers."}},{"n":41,"text":"ततोऽनुयायिभिः सार्धं मरुद्भिरिव वासवः ।\nविदुरान्नानि बुभुजे शुचीनि गुणवन्ति च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, with his followers, like Vasava with the Maruts, he ate Vidura's pure, excellent food."}}]}]}